# user_prog_arena_alloc.tkr — the §16 runtime-prelude injection fixture (crumb I0, RF1). An
# ordinary program (own `src` root, no `teko::runtime`/`teko::sys` source of its own) allocates a
# `[]i64` of 10000 elements, sums them (0..9999 -> 49995000), concatenates "hello", ", ", "world"
# into a 12-char string, and exits 0 only when both hold. Crumb I0 injects the compiler-shipped
# Teko arena + `teko::sys` into this program's file set, so its emitted `teko.c` defines
# `teko_teko__runtime__region_alloc` while allocations still route to the C arena (the injected
# arena is dormant until the crumb E flip). Exit 0 proves the injection is behavior-transparent.

Feature: user_prog_arena_alloc — §16 crumb I0 injects the Teko arena into an ordinary program transparently

  Scenario: ordinary_program_allocates_sums_and_exits_zero — with the runtime prelude injected, a normal allocating program still builds and exits 0
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
